  "lineage": "Metrical psalmody of the Reformed church of Geneva: the Genevan Psalter, completed in 1562, set the French verse psalms of Clément Marot and Théodore de Bèze to 125 melodies, many of them by Louis Bourgeois, for unaccompanied congregational singing in unison. Claude Goudimel's four-part settings of 1564 brought the tunes into domestic and choral use, and the melodies spread with the Huguenots in France and to Reformed churches in the Netherlands and beyond.",
